    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A sharifian dynasty from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/draa-river">Draa</a> valley that ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marrakesh">Marrakesh</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fez">Fez</a> between 1510 and 1659.</li><li>It won the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-alcacer-quibir">Battle of Alcácer Quibir</a> in 1578, where three kings died, and kept <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a> outside the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a>.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmad-al-mansur">Ahmad al-Mansur</a> grew rich on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a> and Saharan gold and conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/songhai-empire">Songhai</a>, but his death in 1603 opened a ruinous civil war.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>In 1612 the library of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> Zidan, sent by ship to safety during the civil war, was seized by Spanish vessels and ended up in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/el-escorial">Escorial</a>, where much of it remains.</p></aside>
    </section>

